# Grid Domain Rules

`docs/grid-rulebook.md` is the source of truth for grid behavior.

- Keep pure grid core modules free of React, DOM, Canvas, and browser APIs.
- Never use `Math.random()` for generation. All random choices go through the seeded PRNG so the same config produces the same cells.
- Generated geometry is logical data only. Do not write render offsets like `+0.5` into `GridCell` data.
- New config fields need defaults, normalization, and tests.
- New hard invariants need validation in `validate.ts`, generator enforcement, and focused tests.
- Gap masks are hard exclusions at base-grid resolution. Keep mask resizing and normalized rows/columns in sync.
